{{!< default}}

<section class="info-hero">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <div class="page-identity">
      <img class="page-identity-mark" src="{{asset "images/download (25).jpg"}}" alt="Garcia Law Office and Notary Public seal logo">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">A clearer start to your legal concern.</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="info-lede">These answers explain how to prepare and what to expect. The right advice depends on the facts and documents of each matter.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details open>
        <summary>What should I bring to an initial consultation?</summary>
        <p>Bring a valid ID and the documents connected to your concern, such as contracts, notices, receipts, titles, messages, or court papers. A short timeline of important events is also useful.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I ask about fees before meeting?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Fees and scope depend on the nature, complexity, urgency, and service requested. The office can discuss the expected next step and applicable fees after learning more about the matter.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you provide notarial services?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Notarial work may include affidavits, acknowledgments, contracts, authorizations, and other documents requiring notarization. Bring the complete document and the required identification.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does sending a message create an attorney-client relationship?</summary>
        <p>No. Online messages are for initial coordination only. An attorney-client relationship is created only when the office formally accepts the engagement.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if my concern is urgent?</summary>
        <p>Call the office and explain the deadline or immediate risk. If there is an immediate danger to life or safety, contact the appropriate emergency authorities first.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What types of legal matters may the office assist with?</summary>
        <p>The office may assist with consultations, contracts and agreements, document review, notarial services, property concerns, family matters, business questions, negotiation, and formal representation when appropriate.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I send documents before my consultation?</summary>
        <p>You may send a short summary and relevant document details through the office's available contact channels. Do not send highly sensitive information until the office confirms the appropriate way to share it.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are online consultations available?</summary>
        <p>Online coordination may be possible depending on the matter, documents, schedule, and technology available. Contact the office to confirm whether an online consultation is suitable.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What identification is needed for notarization?</summary>
        <p>Bring an acceptable government-issued identification card and the complete document. The names and details must be checked carefully, and witnesses or additional records may be required depending on the document.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is my information kept confidential?</summary>
        <p>Information is handled with discretion and used for initial coordination and legal assistance as appropriate. Please avoid sending unnecessary sensitive details through public or unsecured channels.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{@site.url}}/contact/">Request an appointment</a>
  </div>
</section>
